# The new-only checks' failures on record (checks.py --known, oldnew.py --known),
# as of 2026-11-20 (F1): fork main b635486 and feat/sched 72cee59, the 8x and the
# SWGT024, rtlsim 999584e (--control). One a line (oldnew.load_known()):
#   <scenario glob>[,<scenario glob>...]: <check glob> (<= <n> ms|s [by cli <commands>|*] | unbounded)   # why
# A failure is KNOWN only in the scenarios named and within the ceiling (a long
# step's maximum, a gap check's largest gap over its upper bound); above it, it
# FAILs. A gap under a lower bound always FAILs. A saturated long step (>400ms)
# needs `by cli ...`: bounded by the longest console reply (firmware time, typed
# to prompt) of every command the scenario typed, the named ones required; or
# `unbounded`. A line with no ceiling must say `unbounded`.
# Ceilings: the worst measured on either board, rounded up. A line that names a
# scenario run but matched no failed check is flagged: a fix shows as a stale line.
#
# feat/sched at 72cee59 fails none: the two lines left are fork main's alone (the
# old side of oldnew, or checks.py on b635486); on a feat/sched image they are
# flagged as matched by nothing, which is right. The long-step lines (CLI_RUN,
# HOUSE_SEC, RX_STEP) are gone: no step over 20 ms but FL_ERASE in any of the 17
# scenarios on either board (doc/sched/evidence/f1-acceptance.txt).
lacp_l2: lacp gap <= 4 s		# fork main: `l2` prints 1000 entries in one go, 3.86 s without a LACPDU; fixed in feat/sched by E1 (chunked CLI)
stp_upload: stp hello <= 3 s		# fork main: the upload's flash writes hold the loop, no BPDU for 2.84 s; fixed in feat/sched by E3 (the flash job)
